OVERVIEW
This dataset contains processed Wordle gameplay data derived from emoji-based summaries of player attempts. 

Formal citation: Scarcalvetsis. (2022). Wordle games [Data set]. Kaggle https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/scarcalvetsis/wordle-games

ORIGINAL KAGGLE VARIABLES

1. Game
Type: Integer / ID
Unique identifier assigned by Wordle to each daily puzzle. Each value corresponds to a specific target word.

2. Trial
Type: Integer
Number of attempts made by the player before either solving the puzzle or reaching the maximum allowed number of guesses.
Range: 1–6

3. Username
Type: Integer / ID
An anonymized unique identifier for each player in the dataset. No personal identifying information is included.

4. processed_text
Type: String
Emoji-based representation of each Wordle game. Each row contains a sequence of colored square emojis representing individual guesses:
    🟩 = Correct letter in correct position (green)
    🟨 = Correct letter in incorrect position (yellow)
    ⬛ / ⬜ = Incorrect letter (gray/black)

Ex: 

'⬛⬛🟨⬛⬛',
'⬛⬛🟩🟨⬛',
'🟩⬛🟩⬛⬛',
'🟩🟩🟩🟩🟩'



5. target
Type: String
The correct word that the player is attempting to guess for a given game.


DERIVED VARIABLES (shared with the synthetic dataset)

6. n_guesses
Type: Integer
Description: Total number of guesses made by the player in a game.
Range: 1–6

7. entropy_start
Type: Float
Shannon entropy of the candidate solution set at the beginning of the game. Represents the initial uncertainty about the target word.

8. entropy_end
Type: Float
Shannon entropy of the remaining candidate solution set after the final guess. Reflects the uncertainty remaining at the end of the game.

9. mean_entropy_drop
Type: Float
Average reduction in entropy between consecutive guesses. Measures the typical amount of information gained per guess.

10. max_entropy_drop
Type: Float
Largest single reduction in entropy observed during the game. Represents the most informative guess made.

11. early_entropy_drop
Type: Float
Average entropy reduction across the first two guesses. Captures how quickly the player reduces uncertainty early in the game.

12. monotone_entropy_drop
Type: Boolean (True/False)
Indicates whether entropy decreased consistently over the course of the game.
Values:
    True  = Entropy consistently decreases or remains non-increasing across guesses
    False = At least one step shows no decrease or an increase in entropy

13. green_fraction
Type: Float (0–1)
Average proportion of green tiles (correct letter and correct position) across all guesses in a game.

14. yellow_fraction
Type: Float (0–1)
Average proportion of yellow tiles (correct letter but incorrect position) across all guesses in a game.

15. valid
Type: Integer 
Variable created when joining the synthetic dataset; 1 = valid, 0 = invalid (NA for the real dataset)

16. source
Type: String 
Additional differentiator between 'synthetic_valid', 'synthetic_invalid', and 'real'.

